            <ArticleTitle>Penetration of 27- and 30-gauge dental needles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>444-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two types of disposable injection needles were tested clinically for pain of insertion, and penetration resistance. The 30-gauge needle required significantly less force (69 mN) than the 27-gauge needle (139 mN). The difference in pain perception was less remarkable. The author advises that a 30-gauge needle be used in any infiltration injection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
